enerator</span>\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-desc\">Share a strong WiFi password as a scannable code.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"pwg-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/wp-config-generator/\">\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-name\">wp-config.php Generator</span>\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-desc\">Generate salts just as securely.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"pwg-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/json-formatter/\">\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-name\">JSON Formatter</span>\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-desc\">Paste-and-go validation - same privacy promise.</span>\n</a>\n<a class=\"pwg-rel-card\" href=\"%BASE%/tools/bulk-htaccess-redirect/\">\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-name\">Bulk 301 Redirect Generator</span>\n<span class=\"pwg-rel-desc\">Protect URLs people would rather not reach.</span>\n</a>\n</div>\n</section>\n<!-- ═══ 5. FAQ (visible - mirrors the FAQPage schema) ═══ -->\n<section class=\"pwg-faq\" aria-labelledby=\"pwg-faq-h\">\n<h2 id=\"pwg-faq-h\" class=\"pwg-faq-h\">&gt;_ FAQ</h2>\n<details class=\"pwg-faq-item\">\n<summary>Are the passwords generated on my device?</summary>\n<p>Yes. The generator uses the browser’s built-in crypto.getRandomValues - a real cryptographic RNG - and never sends anything to a server, so your password cannot be intercepted in transit.</p>\n</details>\n<details class=\"pwg-faq-item\">\n<summary>How strong is the generated password?</summary>\n<p>The tool reports honestly using Shannon entropy - bits = length × log2(charset) - then penalises for repeated, sequential or keyboard runs and common passwords. A random 20-character password is far stronger than a short one that only looks clever.</p>\n</details>\n<details class=\"pwg-faq-item\">\n<summary>How long should my password be?</summary>\n<p>Aim for 16 characters or more for important accounts. Each added character multiplies the search space, and length matters more than character mix - the meter shows you the entropy and crack time as you adjust length.</p>\n</details>\n</section>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ad-slot ad-slot--in-conte